autocompare-gui: local run (cargo run -p autocompare-gui) — state memory/tmp only, no network; --help for flags
autocompare-gui: desktop client over the comparison engine.

usage:
  autocompare-gui [--open <left> <right> [--tab <name>]] [--screenshot <png>]

flags:
  --open <left> <right>  preload both paths and open the tab
  --tab <name>           text/folder/hex/merge/table/sync/picture/foldermerge/audio (default: text)
  --screenshot <png>     render the fixture PNG headlessly and exit
  --help, -h             print this help and exit
